Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.30,0:00:04.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Computer-use agents have a bad habit. They say “done”. And it's not done.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.96,0:00:10.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,For Holo-3.1, that's 29 of its 51 failures.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.50,0:00:16.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,We wrote it all up in a 30-page paper. First question: can we fix this inside the model?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.94,0:00:27.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,We probed activations, steered them, merged weights, and tried ~15 edits, including AlphaEdit, a closed-form weight edit.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.87,0:00:38.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,A real causal lever, but a blind one. AlphaEdit cuts false successes from 15/16 to 8/16. It also cuts true ones, from 15/16 to 3/16.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.13,0:00:45.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Online, the weight merge gives +1.9 pts, interval [−4.3, +8.0]. No gain.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.26,0:00:51.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Diagnosis: the model does not know when its own “done” is false. So the check has to come from outside.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.84,0:01:00.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everything is public: code, data, and the raw journal of the night. One script re-checks the headline numbers offline.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.72,0:01:13.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we built Feci Guard, an outside judge. Same task, two real virtual machines: Holo alone, and Holo with the Guard.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.08,0:01:18.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,Left says “done”. Official score: 0.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.25,0:01:33.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right says “done” too. Claude checks every requirement on the screen: wrong sheet name, promotions in rows, not columns. Refused. The agent fixes both. Score: 1.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.82,0:01:43.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,The numbers, preregistered. Online, 120 tasks: false “done” 22.5 % → 10.8 %. Significant.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.73,0:01:50.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,With Holo4 as the repairer (replay): 11 of 18 solved, vs 2 without the Guard.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.70,0:01:55.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Feci Guard. The agent says “done”. Now, someone checks.
